$header
# $entity

Project of the system `$entity`, generated by openspacehdl $version from `$source`.

## Files

| Path | What it is |
| --- | --- |
| `$source` | The system, saved by the Open Space Composer |
| `hdl/` | Its export (Export HDL of the Composer): top level, compile order, constraints, address map |
| `sim/run.py` | The VUnit simulation (yours) |
| `sim/tb/${entity}_tb.vhd` | The system testbench with its test cases (yours) |
| `sim/tb/${entity}_th.vhd`, `sim/tb/${entity}_th_pkg.vhd` | The harness and its package (generated) |
| `.openspacehdl/project.json` | The manifest of the generated files |

## Simulate

```shell
pip install openspacehdl[vunit]
python sim/run.py -p 2
```

## After a change of the system

Save the system in the Composer over `$source`, export the HDL into `hdl/`, then:

```shell
openspacehdl update
```

`update` regenerates the generated files. A generated file you edited stays as it is; the new text goes to
`<file>.new` and `update` lists it. Your files (this README, `sim/run.py`, the testbench) are never changed.
